{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"03a4f86b50254288","name":"card_unit_short_wellington","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_short_wellington","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"WELLINGTON","text":"If in your hand, this unit costs 2 less each time you give an order.","flavorText":"The Vickers Wellington was a British medium bomber that was used by RAF and other Commonwealth air forces during WWII. The aircraft was first introduced in the mid 1930s and at the outbreak of WWII the first RAF bomb attack on German targets involved Wellington’s as well as Blenheim bombers. At that time the Wellingtons flew bomber missions unescorted, and in daytime, but when RAF realized how vulnerable they were against defending fighters they quickly switched them to night operations. Throughout the war the Wellingtons were mainly used in night operations and mainly to bomb Axis communications and industrial targets  instead of military targets. Coastal Command also used the Wellingtons variants, mainly in anti-submarine and anti-shipping warfare, but also to perform reconnaissance missions. A total of 11,464 Wellingtons were built, including many variants and prototypes that were used for various purposes.","faction":"Britain","type":"bomber","rarity":"Unique","cost":7,"operationCost":3,"attack":4,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_short_wellington","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_short_wellington_title","SourceString":"WELLINGTON","LocalizedString":"WELLINGTON"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":4,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_short_wellington_text","SourceString":"If in your hand, this unit costs 2 less each time you give an order.","LocalizedString":"If in your hand, this unit costs 2 less each time you give an order."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_short_wellington_history","SourceString":"The Vickers Wellington was a British medium bomber that was used by RAF and other Commonwealth air forces during WWII. The aircraft was first introduced in the mid 1930s and at the outbreak of WWII the first RAF bomb attack on German targets involved Wellington’s as well as Blenheim bombers. At that time the Wellingtons flew bomber missions unescorted, and in daytime, but when RAF realized how vulnerable they were against defending fighters they quickly switched them to night operations. Throughout the war the Wellingtons were mainly used in night operations and mainly to bomb Axis communications and industrial targets  instead of military targets. Coastal Command also used the Wellingtons variants, mainly in anti-submarine and anti-shipping warfare, but also to perform reconnaissance missions. A total of 11,464 Wellingtons were built, including many variants and prototypes that were used for various purposes.","LocalizedString":"The Vickers Wellington was a British medium bomber that was used by RAF and other Commonwealth air forces during WWII. The aircraft was first introduced in the mid 1930s and at the outbreak of WWII the first RAF bomb attack on German targets involved Wellington’s as well as Blenheim bombers. At that time the Wellingtons flew bomber missions unescorted, and in daytime, but when RAF realized how vulnerable they were against defending fighters they quickly switched them to night operations. Throughout the war the Wellingtons were mainly used in night operations and mainly to bomb Axis communications and industrial targets  instead of military targets. Coastal Command also used the Wellingtons variants, mainly in anti-submarine and anti-shipping warfare, but also to perform reconnaissance missions. A total of 11,464 Wellingtons were built, including many variants and prototypes that were used for various purposes."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isR